title: Factional Work in the Districts
subtitle: Congress delegates are chosen in the districts. Win the districts and you win the congress.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: rf_party
view-if: rf_district_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; rf_district_timer = 2

= Factional Work in the Districts

Each faction has its strongholds. Your organisers can work where you are already strong, or try to break into a rival's ground.

- @berlin: Berlin-Brandenburg, the Left's fortress.
- @hamburg: The Wasserkante around Hamburg, Thälmann's home ground.
- @saxony: Saxony, the heartland of the Right.
- @ruhr: The occupied Ruhr, where the members are new and angry.

@berlin
on-arrival: {!
var gain = Q.player == 'left' ? 6 : 3;
Q[Q.player + '_strength'] += gain;
if (Q.player != 'left') { Q.left_dissent += 4; }
!}

[? if player == "left" : Berlin closes ranks behind Fischer and Maslow. ?][? if player != "left" : You win some Berlin cells, and the Left accuses you of poaching. ?]

@hamburg
on-arrival: {!
var gain = Q.player == 'stalin' ? 6 : 3;
Q[Q.player + '_strength'] += gain;
if (Q.player != 'stalin') { Q.stalin_dissent += 4; }
Q.readiness += 1;
!}

The dockers and shipyard workers of Hamburg are among the most militant in Germany. [? if player == "stalin" : Thälmann is one of them, and they know it. ?]

@saxony
on-arrival: {!
var gain = Q.player == 'right' ? 6 : 3;
Q[Q.player + '_strength'] += gain;
if (Q.player != 'right') { Q.right_dissent += 4; }
Q.spd_relation += 1;
!}

Saxony's KPD works closely with the left-wing SPD of the state. [? if player == "right" : It is your base, and it holds. ?][? if player != "right" : Your people make headway, and Brandler's supporters complain. ?]

@ruhr
on-arrival: {!
Q.members += 10;
Q.rev_situation += 2;
Q[Q.player + '_strength'] += 2;
!}

The occupation and the inflation are bringing thousands of new members into the Ruhr locals. They owe no loyalty to any faction yet.
